From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:09:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2835-sdhostd: driver for the sdhost SD card controller

New driver for the BCM2835 sdhost controller, the one Linux uses for the
card slot. Routes GPIO 48-53 to it, initializes the card and serves it as
a disk scheme, `disk.mmc` or the name given as first argument.

Not started at boot yet: bcm2835-sdhcid keeps the card. Start it by hand
as `bcm2835-sdhostd disk.sdhost` to test it next to the old driver; with
an argument it stays in the foreground instead of notifying init.
